        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-09-01/html/CREC-2026-09-01-pt1-PgH5395.htm",
        "start": 5283,
        "quote": "Since then, the State of Maine, the industry, and other scientific \nand research bodies have made progress, investing more than $90 million \nin research. However, it is clear that more time is needed to gather \nthe necessary data and incorporate it into final regulations. \nRepresentative Lawler's bill would provide MMPA and ESA coverage for \nthese fisheries through 2035, providing the necessary time to get these \nregulations right without the threat of more frivolous litigation.",
        "summary": "Since then, the State of Maine, the industry, and other scientific and research bodies have made progress, investing more than $90 million in research. However, it is clear that more time is needed to gather the necessary data and incorporate it into final regulations. Representative Lawler's bill would provide MMPA and ESA coverage for these fisheries through 2035, providing the necessary time to get these regulations right without the threat of more frivolous litigation.",
        "index": 44,
        "reason": "manager-supported need for more time, better data, and protection from frivolous litigation"
